exercises.prompt:
Here nesting does more. What prints?

age = 20
has_ticket = False
if age >= 18:
    if has_ticket:
        print("Enter")
    else:
        print("Buy a ticket")
else:
    print("Too young")

Rewrite the 'Enter only when both True' rule as a single condition:

if age >= 18 ____ has_ticket:
    print("Enter")

What prints?

member = True
age = 70
if member:
    print("Free entry")
else:
    if age >= 65:
        print("Half price")
    else:
        print("Full price")
